This test verifies TLS Server Name Indication (SNI) without using the
public network.

The test starts a QCA-based TLS server on the IPv4 loopback interface and
connects to it using several logical TLS host names.  The server selects a
different certificate after QCA::TLS::hostNameReceived() for every host.
The client verifies the selected certificate against the local test CA.

The certificates and private keys in certs/ are test fixtures only.  They
are valid from 2020 through 2120 and must never be used outside the test
suite.
